{"builder":"Add a --shout flag to the greet CLI (issue https://github.com/o/greet-cli/issues/12) in one pull request.\n\nContext: bin/greet.js takes the first argument that does not start with `--` as the name and prints `greeting(name)` from src/greet.js (`Hello, <name>!`) plus a newline. Tests are in test/greet.test.js and run with `npm test` (node --test). .github/workflows/pages.yml publishes the docs/ directory to GitHub Pages on push to main.\n\nSteps:\n1. In bin/greet.js, detect `--shout` anywhere in `process.argv.slice(2)`. When it is present, print the greeting converted to upper case (e.g. `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` prints `HELLO, ADA!` followed by a newline). `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` should behave the same. Keep the name-detection logic so `--shout` is never taken as the name, and keep the usage error when no name is given.\n2. Without `--shout`, output must stay exactly as today: `node bin/greet.js Ada` prints `Hello, Ada!\\n`. Do not change src/greet.js's `greeting` output.\n3. Add tests to test/greet.test.js: one for `--shout Ada` giving `HELLO, ADA!\\n`, and keep the existing `cli` test (no flag) passing unchanged. Run `npm test` and make sure all tests pass.\n4. Update docs/index.md to document `--shout`: show the usage (e.g. `node bin/greet.js --shout <name>`) and say it prints the greeting in upper case. Leave the docs/ directory as the Pages source and do not alter .github/workflows/pages.yml in a way that stops it publishing docs/ on push to main, so the published page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ will list --shout after merge.\n5. Open the pull request, referencing issue #12.","verifier":"Run every command from the repository root at the PR head. Each command below is self-contained.\n\nCheck 1 — \"node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\"\nRun: `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada`\nThe greeting for Ada (without the flag) is `Hello, Ada!`, so its upper case is `HELLO, ADA!`.\nPASS: stdout, ignoring a trailing newline, is `HELLO, ADA!`.\nFAIL: stdout is anything else (e.g. `Hello, Ada!`, mixed case, a usage error, or `--shout` treated as the name).\n\nCheck 2 — \"without --shout the output is unchanged\"\nRun: `node bin/greet.js Ada` and also `git show HEAD:bin/greet.js >/dev/null && node -e \"process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(require('child_process').execFileSync('node',['bin/greet.js','Ada'],{encoding:'utf8'})))\"`\nBefore this change the CLI printed `Hello, Ada!` followed by a newline (see the existing `cli` test in test/greet.test.js, which expects `Hello, Ada!\\n`).\nPASS: `node bin/greet.js Ada` prints exactly `Hello, Ada!` followed by a newline (JSON output `\"Hello, Ada!\\n\"`).\nFAIL: the output differs in any way (case, text, extra or missing characters).\n\nCheck 3 — \"docs/index.md documents --shout\"\nRun: `grep -n -- '--shout' docs/index.md` and read docs/index.md.\nPASS: docs/index.md mentions `--shout` and describes what it does (upper-case / louder greeting).\nFAIL: docs/index.md does not mention `--shout`, or mentions it with no description of its effect.\n\nCheck 4 — \"after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\"\nThe live page can only be seen after merge; do not fetch it. Check what the head contains that will produce it.\nRun: `cat .github/workflows/pages.yml` and `grep -n -- '--shout' docs/index.md`\nPASS: .github/workflows/pages.yml still publishes the docs directory to GitHub Pages on push to main (upload-pages-artifact with path docs, then deploy-pages), and docs/index.md at the head lists `--shout`.\nFAIL: the workflow no longer publishes docs/ on push to main, or docs/index.md at the head does not list `--shout`.\n\nAdvisory\n- Run `npm test`; all tests should pass, and there should be a test covering `--shout`.\n- Also try `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` (flag after name) — it should print `HELLO, ADA!`.\n- `node bin/greet.js --shout` with no name should still print the usage error and exit with status 2.\n- Exit status of `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` should be 0."}